From d8e3e15aeefda8de67d5b336ca0591e60dbc9971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jdbencardinop <jdbencardinop@unal.edu.co>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:13:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(verify): root V7/V8 shadow at recorded base for
 committed-range captures

runClosureReplay always rooted the shared V7/V8 shadow at live HEAD. For a
committed-range capture (--auto/--from+--to/--commit-range), the target's
own commits land between the recorded status.apply.base_commit and HEAD,
so a HEAD-rooted shadow already contains the feature's change and both
replaying the recipe (V7) and running "git apply --check" against the
canonical patch (V8) double-apply it. V8 fails because the patch's context
no longer matches a tree that already has the change (GH #3).

Root cause: shadow-root selection never consulted capture provenance.

Fix:
- resolveClosureShadowRoot roots the shadow at the recorded base_commit
  whenever the feature's latest patch-generations.json generation has
  upper.kind "commit"/"range" (the committed-range family), and fails
  verify explicitly (never a silent HEAD fallback) when that base_commit
  is empty, unresolvable, or not reachable from HEAD.
- Working-tree/staged/unstaged captures, and any feature predating
  patch-generations.json, are unaffected and keep replaying against live
  HEAD exactly as before -- this is the existing, correct drift-detection
  behavior for those capture modes.
- parentAlreadyInShadowBaseline extends the same provenance-trust rule to
  hard parents: a parent's recipe is skipped (not double-replayed) when
  the parent's own recorded committed-range landing commit is already
  reachable from the chosen shadow root, mirroring the existing
  upstream_merged skip.

Tests: new internal/workflow/verify_committed_range_test.go covers the
GH #3 reproduction (committed-range, no parents, V8 now passes against
the recorded base instead of double-applying against HEAD), an invalid
canonical patch still failing V8 against the recorded base (no
weakening of V8 into a skip/success-shaped fallback), an unreachable/
invalid recorded base_commit failing verify explicitly, and a hard
parent already represented in the recorded base being skipped instead
of double-replayed. All four new tests were confirmed to fail without
the fix (git stash of verify.go) and pass with it. Every pre-existing
V0-V9/closure-replay/CLI/integration test still passes unchanged.

Verified against the real reproduction: built bin/tpatch fresh from
this worktree and ran "tpatch verify editable-provider-neutral-threads
--path .../worktrees/thread-store". Verdict flipped from failed
(post_apply_patch_replay_clean only) to passed/exit 0, with no changes
to Tuicr source (src/) -- only the feature's status.json verify overlay
and the auto-generated FEATURES.md dashboard were touched, both normal
"tpatch verify" side effects.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
